<title>USA: Cross-Continent Auto IPO surges at opening.</title>
<headline>Cross-Continent Auto IPO surges at opening.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Cross-Continent Auto Retailers Inc surged on the New York Stock Exchange after the company's initial public offering on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The company's shares rose six to 20 from its initial public offering price of $14. Morgan Stanley was the lead underwriter of the offering.</p>
